                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "[h1]Game Dev Tycoon[/h1]\n\n[b]Started in a garage.\n\nEnded up emotionally dependent on review scores from four imaginary critics.[/b]\n\nGame Dev Tycoon is dangerously simple.\n\nMake a game.\n\nPick a genre.\n\nPick a topic.\n\nMove some sliders.\n\nRelease it.\n\nWatch the reviews come in.\n\nEither become rich...\n\nor immediately question every decision you've ever made.\n\n[b]\"This combination should work.\"[/b]\n\n5/10.\n\n[b]\"Okay, I'll improve the engine.\"[/b]\n\n6/10.\n\n[b]\"Fine, I'll spend all my research points and make the perfect sequel.\"[/b]\n\n4/10.\n\nExcellent.\n\nWhat makes the game so addictive is the progression.\n\nYou start alone in a tiny garage making garbage for ancient computers, then slowly hire employees, create better engines, research new technology, move into larger offices, and eventually become the exact kind of giant game company you probably complained about five minutes earlier.\n\nThe management loop is simple, but it works.\n\nFiguring out which genres, topics, platforms and development priorities fit together is genuinely satisfying once you start understanding the system.\n\nMy biggest complaint is that the review scores can sometimes feel completely arbitrary.\n\nYou can make something that looks perfect on paper and somehow receive the gaming equivalent of:\n\n[i]\"It's okay.\"[/i]\n\nThen another game you made while half-paying attention becomes a 10/10 masterpiece.\n\n[b]So basically, an accurate simulation of the games industry.[/b]\n\nThe campaign also moves pretty quickly. Sometimes I wish the years slowed down a little so I had more time to experiment before the entire gaming industry moved on without me.\n\nBut after nearly 20 hours, I completely understand why people keep coming back to it.\n\n[h1]9/10[/h1]\n\n[b]Simple, addictive, and surprisingly hard to put down.[/b]\n\n[i]Spent millions developing my dream game.\n\nCritics gave it a 6.\n\nNow I understand game developers.[/i]",
